Subject: [PATCH] 288: REPAIR_OK on the first honest run - and the refused
 reward ranks arms backwards

The min>=3 full run passes all seven gates. Held out: forgery detection 0.683
against the counting detector's 0.387 and a random floor of 0.213; on the
duplicated forgery 0.831 against 0.254, where counting is wrong by
construction; clean-margin AUC 0.672 at +4.09 sigma; repair reward 0.433
against majority-of-the-rest at 0.049; UNKNOWN margin AUC 0.622 at +2.18
sigma. That is the first time a stage in this project has passed its own
examiners end to end, and the examiners are the strict ones - matched floors,
derived thresholds, a control on the training tape.

The refused reward earned its refusal, and not by argument. verdict_restored -
"is the world more consistent by the judges", kept as an observer only -
ranks the two arms EXACTLY BACKWARDS:

  min3   repair reward   model 0.433 vs votes 0.049   observer 0.507 vs 0.775
  min2   repair reward   model 0.085 vs votes 0.184   observer 0.842 vs 0.803

Trained on that signal we would have selected the broken arm and called it
progress. It stays an observer, and now it has a measurement saying why
rather than a story.

And my min>=2 change was half wrong, in a way this project has now hit four
times. It helped detection - dup detection rose 0.831 to 0.940 - and it broke
repair, because a two-mention address always leaves exactly one survivor:

  {A,A} forged -> keep [A], original A   -> the answer is that candidate
  {A,B} forged -> keep [A], original B   -> the answer is UNKNOWN

Identical input, opposite labels. Undecidable, so answering always is optimal
and the head learned precisely that: repair coverage 0.966 against min3's
0.535, and G_repairs false. Failure mode 12 - a target that is not a function
of the input - arriving through a change I made to fix a different problem.

The fix keeps both halves: detection still sees every two-mention address,
repair is trained and scored only where at least two values survive, and the
skipped count is reported as single_candidate_skipped so the restriction is
visible rather than assumed. That is 286's --min-candidates lesson applied to
the head it actually belongs to.

Next: the address holdout on this file. min2 detection numbers were the best
measured, so the two-mention addresses are worth keeping for the half of the
task that can use them.

